=== width 80, default
\e[1m\e[3m\e[4:2mMeeting notes, week 42\e[24m\e[23m\e[22m

Attendees: Ada, Grace, Linus. Notes by Ada.

\e[1m\e[4mDecisions\e[24m\e[22m

1. Ship the parser change behind a flag first.
2. Move the nightly build to \e[1m03:00\e[22m UTC.
3. Drop support for the \e[38;5;3mlegacy\e[39m backend after the next release.

\e[1m\e[4mNumbers\e[24m\e[22m

┌───────────────────┬───────────┬───────────┬────────┐
│ \e[1mMetric           \e[22m │ \e[1mLast week\e[22m │ \e[1mThis week\e[22m │ \e[1mChange\e[22m │
├───────────────────┼───────────┼───────────┼────────┤
│ Build time (s)    │       412 │       388 │  -6%   │
├───────────────────┼───────────┼───────────┼────────┤
│ Test failures     │        17 │         9 │  -47%  │
├───────────────────┼───────────┼───────────┼────────┤
│ Open bugs         │        63 │        58 │  -8%   │
├───────────────────┼───────────┼───────────┼────────┤
│ Median review (h) │       5.5 │       4.0 │  -27%  │
└───────────────────┴───────────┴───────────┴────────┘

\e[1m\e[4mSnippets we looked at\e[24m\e[22m

The slow path:

  \e[38;5;5mfn\e[39m \e[38;5;4mlookup\e[39m(\e[38;5;6mmap\e[39m: \e[38;5;5m&\e[39mHashMap<String, Vec<\e[38;5;5mu32\e[39m>>, \e[38;5;6mkey\e[39m: \e[38;5;5m&str\e[39m) -> \e[38;5;5musize\e[39m {
      map.\e[38;5;6mget\e[39m(key).\e[38;5;6mmap\e[39m(|\e[38;5;6mids\e[39m| ids.\e[38;5;6mlen\e[39m()).\e[38;5;6munwrap_or_default\e[39m()
  }

And the shell one-liner that finds the culprit:

  git log\e[38;5;6m --since\e[39m\e[38;5;5m=\e[39m1.week\e[38;5;6m --format\e[39m\e[38;5;5m=\e[39m\e[38;5;2m'%h %s'\e[39m\e[38;5;5m --\e[39m src/parser \e[38;5;5m|\e[39m head\e[38;5;6m -20\e[39m

\e[1m\e[4mOpen questions\e[24m\e[22m

• Who owns the flaky \e[38;5;3mintegration::upload\e[39m test?
• Is the \e[38;5;3m~~old~~\e[39m benchmark data still valid?
• Do we need a \e[3msecond\e[23m staging cluster?

\e[1m\e[4mNext week\e[24m\e[22m

Review the draft at \e[4mhttps://example.com/draft\e[24m and add comments by Friday.
